rcuit court, district court, and other county offices.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Jurisdiction of the Circuit Court</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Anne Arundel County Circuit Court has jurisdiction over a wide range of cases, including criminal, civil, family law, and probate cases. It also hears appeals from lower courts and administrative agencies.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Types of Cases Handled by the Circuit Court</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Anne Arundel County Circuit Court handles various types of cases, including:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>Criminal Cases in the Circuit Court</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The circuit court has jurisdiction over serious criminal cases, including felonies, misdemeanors, and traffic offenses. It also handles juvenile delinquency cases and mental health cases.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>Civil Cases in the Circuit Court</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The circuit court handles civil cases involving disputes between individuals or organizations. Examples of civil cases include contract disputes, personal injury lawsuits, and property disputes.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>Family Law Cases in the Circuit Court</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The circuit court handles family law cases, including divorce, child custody, child support, and adoption cases.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>Probate Cases in the Circuit Court</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The circuit court handles probate cases, including wills, estates, and trusts.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Appeals in the Circuit Court</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Anne Arundel County Circuit Court hears appeals from lower courts and administrative agencies. Appeals can be filed by individuals or organizations who believe they were wrongly convicted or have a dispute with a lower court's decision.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Court Administration and Services</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Anne Arundel County Circuit Court provides various court administration and services, including:</p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"is-layout-constrained\">\n<ul>\n<li>Clerk's office: The clerk's office maintains court records, processes court filings, and provides assistance to the public.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Jury services: The court coordinates and manages jury duty for residents of Anne Arundel County.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Court security: The court has a security team that provides security</li>\n\n\n\n<li>for the courthouse and ensures the safety of judges, staff, and visitors.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Interpreter services: The court provides interpreter services for individuals who require assistance with language translation during court proceedings.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>see also Albany County Family Court</p>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<h2>Jury Duty in the Circuit Court</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Residents of Anne Arundel County may be called for jury duty in the circuit court. The court randomly selects potential jurors from voter registration and driver's license records. Individuals who are selected for jury duty must serve for the duration of the trial.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Court Records in the Circuit Court</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The clerk's office in the Anne Arundel County Circuit Court maintains court records for all cases heard in the court. Individuals can access court records online or in person at the clerk's office. However, certain records may be sealed or restricted from public access. Hours and Location of the Circuit Court</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The Anne Arundel County Circuit Court is located at 8 Church Circle in Annapolis. The courthouse is open from 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. on weekdays, except on state holidays. Contact Information for the Circuit Court</p>\n\n\n\n<p>If you need to contact the Anne Arundel County Circuit Court, you can do so using the following information:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Address: 8 Church Circle, Annapolis, MD 21401</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Phone: (410) 222-1397</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Website: https://www.courts.state.md.us/circuit/annearundel</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2>Anne Arundel County Circuit Court Judges</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Anne Arundel County Circuit Court has several judges who preside over civil, criminal, and family law cases. Some of the current judges include:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Honorable Mark W. Crooks</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Honorable Michael W. Siri</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Honorable Stacy W. McCormack</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Honorable Laura S. Kiessling</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Honorable Glenn L. Klavans</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Honorable Alison L. Asti</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Honorable Donna M. Schaeffer</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2>Anne Arundel County Circuit Court Case Search</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Anne Arundel County Circuit Court provides online access to case information through its Case Search portal. This portal allows users to search for civil, criminal, and traffic cases by case number, party name, and attorney name. Users can also view case dockets and case documents online.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Anne Arundel County Circuit Court Family Division</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Anne Arundel County Circuit Court has a dedicated Family Division that handles a variety of family law cases, including divorce, child custody, child support, and adoption. The Family Division also provides resources and services to help families navigate the legal system and resolve disputes.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Anne Arundel Circuit Court Docket</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Anne Arundel Circuit Court docket is a schedule of all the cases that will be heard by the court on a particular day. The docket includes the case name, case number, parties involved, and the time and location of the hearing.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Anne Arundel County Divorce Records</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Anne Arundel County Circuit Court maintains divorce records for all divorces granted within the county. These records are available to the public and can be obtained through the Circuit Court Clerk's Office.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Anne Arundel County Circuit Court Hours</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Anne Arundel County Circuit Court is open to the public from Monday to Friday, from 8:30 am to 4:30 pm. However, the court may close on holidays and other special occasions.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>see also Sonoma County Superior Court</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Annapolis Courthouse Address</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Annapolis Courthouse, which houses the Anne Arundel County Circuit Court, is located at 8 Church Circle in Annapolis, Maryland.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Annapolis Courthouse Parking</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Parking is available near the Annapolis Courthouse at several parking garages and lots, including the Hillman Garage, the Gotts Garage, and the Park Place Garage. Metered street parking is also available in the surrounding area. However, parking may be limited and expensive during peak hours, so it is advisable to plan ahead and arrive early if possible.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Conclusion</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Anne Arundel County Circuit Court is an important legal institution in Maryland. It has jurisdiction over a wide range of cases, including criminal, civil, family law, and probate cases. The court also handles appeals from lower courts and administrative agencies. With its long history and experienced judges, the Anne Arundel County Circuit Court is committed to providing fair and impartial justice to all residents of the county.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>FAQs</h2>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>How do I file a case in the Anne Arundel County Circuit Court? </strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>To file a case in the Anne Arundel County Circuit Court, you must fill out the appropriate paperwork and pay any required fees. You can obtain the necessary forms and information from the court's website or by visiting the courthouse in person.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Can I pay my fines online for traffic tickets received in the county?</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>Yes, you can pay fines for traffic tickets online through the court's website.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>How do I request an interpreter for a court proceeding?</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>To request an interpreter for a court proceeding, you should contact the court's administrative office in advance of the proceeding to make arrangements.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>How long does jury duty typically last in the circuit court?</strong> </p>\n\n\n\n<p>The length of jury duty in the circuit court can vary depending on the trial. Typically, jurors are required to serve for the duration of the trial.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Can I access court records for free online? </strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>Some court records are available for free online, while others may require a fee or a visit to the clerk's office in person. You can check the court's website or contact the clerk's office for more information.</p>\n",
